 "brief": "A bearing block for a 608 bearing (22 mm OD, 7 mm wide) in SLS PA12. The bearing's axis is\nalong Y through (0, 0, 25), the seat is 22 mm diameter and 7 mm long (y = -3.5 to 3.5); leave at\nleast 4 mm of wall round it and a 12 mm hole through for the shaft. It bolts to a flat base at\nz = 0 with two M5 screws along Z at (+/-30, 0); the screw heads sit on top of 12 mm diameter,\n6 mm tall bosses (z = 0 to 6) and need a 10 mm diameter column clear above each for the socket. The block can\noccupy x = -40 to 40, y = -6 to 6, z = 0 to 42. The shaft pushes on the bearing with up to\n300 N, and the direction depends on the belt so treat it as any direction perpendicular to the\nshaft. Safety factor 2.5.",
